WEBVTT

00:00.630 --> 00:03.660
So we have this larger triangle
here and inside of that,

00:03.660 --> 00:05.670
we have these other
triangles, and we're

00:05.670 --> 00:07.480
given this information
right over here.

00:07.480 --> 00:14.680
That triangle BCD is congruent
to triangle BCA, which

00:14.680 --> 00:18.270
is congruent to triangle ECD.

00:18.270 --> 00:20.420
And given just this
information, what

00:20.420 --> 00:22.130
I want to do in
this drawing, I want

00:22.130 --> 00:25.380
to figure out what every
angle on this drawing is.

00:25.380 --> 00:27.700
What's the measure
of every angle?

00:27.700 --> 00:29.124
So let's see what
we can do here.

00:29.124 --> 00:30.790
So let's just start
with the information

00:30.790 --> 00:32.380
that they've actually given us.

00:32.380 --> 00:40.340
So we know that triangle
BCD is congruent to-- well,

00:40.340 --> 00:42.264
we know all of these
three triangles

00:42.264 --> 00:43.430
are congruent to each other.

00:43.430 --> 00:47.760
So, for example, BCD
is congruent to ECD,

00:47.760 --> 00:50.320
and so their corresponding
sides and corresponding angles

00:50.320 --> 00:51.840
will also be congruent.

00:51.840 --> 00:53.830
So just looking at the
order in which they're

00:53.830 --> 00:58.270
written B, vertex B
corresponds, in this triangle,

00:58.270 --> 01:04.410
BCD, corresponds
to vertex B in BCA,

01:04.410 --> 01:07.610
so this is the B
vertex in BCA, which

01:07.610 --> 01:11.030
corresponds to the
E vertex in ECD.

01:11.030 --> 01:13.530
So all-- everything that
I've done in magenta,

01:13.530 --> 01:16.310
all of these angles
are congruent,

01:16.310 --> 01:20.900
and then we also know
that the C angle.

01:20.900 --> 01:26.930
So in BCA-- sorry, BCD,
this angle right over here,

01:26.930 --> 01:30.706
is congruent to
the C angle in BCA.

01:30.706 --> 01:33.530
BCA, the C angle
is right over here,

01:33.530 --> 01:36.430
or C is the vertex
for that angle in BCA.

01:36.430 --> 01:42.330
And that is also the C angle, I
guess we could call it, in ECD.

01:42.330 --> 01:46.330
But in ECD, we're talking about
this angle right over here.

01:46.330 --> 01:48.845
So these three angles are
going to be congruent.

01:48.845 --> 01:50.620
And I think you could
already guess a way

01:50.620 --> 01:53.180
to come up with the values
of those three angles.

01:53.180 --> 01:54.900
But let's keep looking
at everything else

01:54.900 --> 01:56.170
that they're telling us.

01:56.170 --> 01:59.250
Finally, we have
vertex D over here.

01:59.250 --> 02:03.535
So angle-- so this is the last
one in where we listed-- so

02:03.535 --> 02:08.630
in triangle BCD, this
angle right over here

02:08.630 --> 02:12.440
corresponds to the A
vertex angle in BCA.

02:12.440 --> 02:14.390
So BCA, that's
going to correspond

02:14.390 --> 02:15.812
to this angle right over here.

02:15.812 --> 02:18.020
It's really the only one
that we haven't labeled yet.

02:18.020 --> 02:20.450
And that corresponds
to this angle,

02:20.450 --> 02:22.920
this vertex right over here,
that angle right over there.

02:22.920 --> 02:24.880
And just to make it
consistent, this C

02:24.880 --> 02:26.989
should also be
circled in yellow.

02:26.989 --> 02:28.530
And so we have all
these congruences,

02:28.530 --> 02:32.030
and now we can come up with some
interesting things about them.

02:32.030 --> 02:37.520
First of all, here, angle
BCA, angle BCD, and angle DCE,

02:37.520 --> 02:40.820
they're all congruent, and
when you add them up together,

02:40.820 --> 02:42.130
you get to 180 degrees.

02:42.130 --> 02:44.720
If you put them all adjacent,
as they all are right here,

02:44.720 --> 02:46.260
they end up with
a straight angle,

02:46.260 --> 02:48.040
if you look at
their outer sides.

02:48.040 --> 02:49.759
So you have, if
these are each x,

02:49.759 --> 02:51.300
you have three of
them added together

02:51.300 --> 02:54.750
have to be 180 degrees, which
tells us that each of these

02:54.750 --> 02:56.654
have to be 60 degrees.

02:56.654 --> 02:58.070
That's the only
way you have three

02:58.070 --> 03:00.820
of the same thing adding
up to 180 degrees.

03:00.820 --> 03:02.180
Fair enough.

03:02.180 --> 03:03.820
What else can we do?

03:03.820 --> 03:06.310
Well, we have these
two characters up here.

03:06.310 --> 03:09.110
They are both equal and
they add up to 180 degrees.

03:09.110 --> 03:10.880
They are supplementary,
the only way

03:10.880 --> 03:12.880
you can have two equal
things that add up to 180

03:12.880 --> 03:15.140
is if they're both 90 degrees.

03:15.140 --> 03:17.880
So these two characters
are both 90 degrees.

03:17.880 --> 03:20.560
Or we could say this is a right
angle, that's a right angle.

03:20.560 --> 03:22.185
And this is congruent
to both of those,

03:22.185 --> 03:25.700
so that is also 90
degrees, and then

03:25.700 --> 03:28.244
we're left with these
magenta parts of the angle.

03:28.244 --> 03:29.660
And here, we could
just say, well,

03:29.660 --> 03:33.740
90 plus 60 plus something
is going to add up to 180.

03:33.740 --> 03:36.090
90 plus 60 is 150.

03:36.090 --> 03:38.520
So this has to be 30
degrees to add up to 180.

03:38.520 --> 03:41.280
And if that's 30 degrees,
then this is 30 degrees.

03:41.280 --> 03:44.744
And then this thing right
over here is 30 degrees.

03:44.744 --> 03:46.410
And then the last
thing-- we've actually

03:46.410 --> 03:49.300
done what we said we would do,
we found out all of the angles.

03:49.300 --> 03:51.404
We could also think
about these outer angles.

03:51.404 --> 03:52.820
So this-- or not
the outer angles,

03:52.820 --> 03:54.180
or these combined angles.

03:54.180 --> 03:59.620
So angle say AC-- or say, angle
ABE, so this whole angle we see

03:59.620 --> 04:02.030
is 60 degrees.

04:02.030 --> 04:05.370
This angle is 90 degrees,
and this angle here is 30.

04:05.370 --> 04:08.770
So what's interesting is
these three smaller triangles,

04:08.770 --> 04:11.200
they all have the exact
same angles, 30, 60, 90,

04:11.200 --> 04:14.106
and the exact same side lengths.

04:14.106 --> 04:15.730
We know that because
they're congruent.

04:15.730 --> 04:18.313
And what's interesting is when
you put them together this way,

04:18.313 --> 04:21.320
they construct this larger
triangle, triangle ABE,

04:21.320 --> 04:22.590
that's clearly not congruent.

04:22.590 --> 04:23.640
It's a larger triangle.

04:23.640 --> 04:26.320
It has different
measures for its lengths,

04:26.320 --> 04:30.250
but it has the same angles
30, 60, and then 90.

04:30.250 --> 04:32.250
So it's actually similar
to all of the triangles

04:32.250 --> 04:34.600
that it's made up of.
